IMPORT prelude

-- Code of Massachusetts Regulations, 106 CMR 704.000 (Department of Transitional Assistance): financial eligibility for
-- Transitional Aid to Families with Dependent Children (TAFDC), Massachusetts's TANF cash assistance. The income test
-- (704.260); the work-related-expense deduction (704.270); the dependent care deduction (704.275); the earned income
-- disregards at application (704.280) and for the grant (704.281); the need and payment standards (704.410, 704.420, with
-- the figures the Department posts for them); the grant calculation (704.500(A)); and the duty of a person whose income is
-- deemed to the family to report changes within ten days (704.235(B)(1)).
--
-- SEAT: the parent or caretaker who applies for, or receives, TAFDC for the family: "Is my family's income low enough? How
-- much TAFDC will we get each month?" Steps the Department performs are encoded as what they give the family.
--
-- Edition: 106 CMR 704.000 as posted on Mass.gov on 24 October 2026 (pages dated 5/10/24), and the Table of Need and
-- Payment Standards posted by the Department for 704.410 and 704.420 (retrieved the same day), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/106-cmr-704-transitional-cash-assistance-financial-eligibility.txt and
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/tafdc-table-of-need-and-payment-standards-704410-704420.txt.
--
-- The statute (M.G.L. c. 118) is not deposited: malegislature.gov did not answer the fetcher (see the Massachusetts README).
-- Which income is countable or noncountable (704.210, 704.250), who is in the filing and assistance units (704.300 to
-- 704.330), whether the unit gets the rent allowance (106 CMR 705.910, not deposited), the Federal Poverty Limit, and good
-- cause (106 CMR 701.380, not deposited) are asked as facts.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: EAEDC (704.285, 704.286, 704.430 to 704.440, 704.500(B)); assets and transfers (704.110 to 704.135); deemed
-- income amounts (704.230 to 704.236); lump sums (704.240); self-employment and the wage averaging rules (704.290); earned
-- income of more than one member of the assistance unit (the other members' countable earnings are one input).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `TAFDC financial eligibility and grant -- 106 CMR 704.000`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `Step 7 of 106 CMR 704.500(A) states no amount when the result equals the Payment Standard, which happens when the family has no countable income (NOTES.md finding 1)`

§§ `704.410, 704.420 -- the Need and Payment Standards`

-- The posted table (deposited): one column "A. Need and Payment Standard, No Rent Allowance" and one "B. ... With Rent
-- Allowance", so for each size the Need Standard and the Payment Standard are the same figure. Size 1: $564 / $604; 2: 713
-- / 753; 3: 861 / 901; 4: 1,003 / 1,043; 5: 1,150 / 1,190; 6: 1,301 / 1,341; 7: 1,448 / 1,488; 8: 1,593 / 1,633; 9: 1,738
-- / 1,788; 10: 1,885 / 1,925; "Incremental 153.00 153.00" for each person above 10. In September 2026 the standard "shall
-- be increased by $500 for each eligible applicant and client under age 19".
GIVEN `assistance unit size` IS A NUMBER
      `with rent allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the posted standard` MEANS
    IF `with rent allowance`
    THEN BRANCH
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 1  THEN 604
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 2  THEN 753
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 3  THEN 901
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 4  THEN 1043
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 5  THEN 1190
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 6  THEN 1341
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 7  THEN 1488
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 8  THEN 1633
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 9  THEN 1788
            OTHERWISE 1925 PLUS 153 TIMES (`assistance unit size` MINUS 10)
    ELSE BRANCH
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 1  THEN 564
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 2  THEN 713
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 3  THEN 861
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 4  THEN 1003
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 5  THEN 1150
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 6  THEN 1301
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 7  THEN 1448
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 8  THEN 1593
            IF `assistance unit size` EQUALS 9  THEN 1738
            OTHERWISE 1885 PLUS 153 TIMES (`assistance unit size` MINUS 10)

GIVEN `assistance unit size` IS A NUMBER
      `with rent allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is September 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members under 19` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Need and Payment Standard` MEANS
    IF `the month is September 2026`
    THEN (`the posted standard` `assistance unit size` `with rent allowance`) PLUS 500 TIMES `members under 19`
    ELSE `the posted standard` `assistance unit size` `with rent allowance`

@export What is the TAFDC Need and Payment Standard for my family (106 CMR 704.410, 704.420)?
GIVEN `family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TAFDC assistance unit
      `rent allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your assistance unit gets the rent allowance (generally, if you live in private, unsubsidized housing and pay rent)
      `September 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the month asked about is September 2026 (the month of the $500 clothing allowance for each child under 19)
      `children under 19` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible members of the assistance unit are under 19
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Need and Payment Standard` MEANS
    `the Need and Payment Standard` `family size` `rent allowance` `September 2026` `children under 19`

§§ `704.270, 704.275, 704.280, 704.281 -- deductions and disregards from my earnings`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

-- 704.275(A): for full-time work, "the actual cost of dependent care ... but shall not exceed $175 per dependent child, age
-- two or older, or incapacitated individual per month. For children under the age of two ... $200." Less than full-time:
-- the table by monthly hours: 1-43, $44 / $50; 44-87, $88 / $100; 88-130, $132 / 150; 131 and above, $175 / $200. "In all
-- situations, the amount allowed ... is the actual expenditure ... or the maximum allowable deduction, whichever is less."
GIVEN `monthly hours worked` IS A NUMBER
      `children two or older in care` IS A NUMBER
      `children under two in care` IS A NUMBER
      `actual monthly cost of dependent care` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent care deduction` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `actual monthly cost of dependent care` `the maximum`
    WHERE
        `the maximum` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `monthly hours worked` LESS THAN 1   THEN 0
                IF `monthly hours worked` AT MOST 43    THEN (44 TIMES `children two or older in care`) PLUS (50 TIMES `children under two in care`)
                IF `monthly hours worked` AT MOST 87    THEN (88 TIMES `children two or older in care`) PLUS (100 TIMES `children under two in care`)
                IF `monthly hours worked` AT MOST 130   THEN (132 TIMES `children two or older in care`) PLUS (150 TIMES `children under two in care`)
                OTHERWISE (175 TIMES `children two or older in care`) PLUS (200 TIMES `children under two in care`)

DECLARE `My earnings` HAS
    `gross monthly earned income`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `monthly hours worked`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `children two or older in care`                                IS A NUMBER
    `children under two in care`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `actual monthly cost of dependent care`                        IS A NUMBER
    `reduced or quit work, or refused a job, without good cause`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `failed to report income on time without good cause`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in the Full Employment Program`                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- 704.280: at application, "an applicant who has received TAFDC within the last four calendar months is eligible to have 50%
-- of the remaining gross earned income disregarded, after work-related-expenses, but before dependent care deductions,
-- unless" (A) income reduced, work ended or a job refused without good cause, (B) failure to report on time without good
-- cause, (C) employment in FEP, (D) liable for the child but not in the case (out of scope: the earner here is in the case).
-- 704.270(A): "An employed applicant is entitled to a $200 monthly work-related-expense deduction from gross wages in
-- determining eligibility"; (B)(1): not one who meets 704.280(A) or (B). 704.275(B)(1): no dependent care deduction for one
-- who meets 704.280(A) or (B).
GIVEN `e` IS A `My earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 704.280(A) or (B) condition applies` IF
        `e`'s `reduced or quit work, or refused a job, without good cause`
    OR  `e`'s `failed to report income on time without good cause`

GIVEN `e` IS A `My earnings`
      `received TAFDC within the last four calendar months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my countable earnings for the income test` MEANS
    IF `a 704.280(A) or (B) condition applies` `e`
    THEN `e`'s `gross monthly earned income`
    ELSE `the larger of` 0 (`after the disregard` MINUS `the dependent care deduction` (`e`'s `monthly hours worked`) (`e`'s `children two or older in care`) (`e`'s `children under two in care`) (`e`'s `actual monthly cost of dependent care`))
    WHERE
        `after the work-related expense` MEANS `the larger of` 0 (`e`'s `gross monthly earned income` MINUS 200)
        `the 50% disregard applies` MEANS
                `received TAFDC within the last four calendar months`
            AND (NOT (`e`'s `employed in the Full Employment Program`))
        `after the disregard` MEANS
            IF `the 50% disregard applies`
            THEN `after the work-related expense` TIMES 50%
            ELSE `after the work-related expense`

-- 704.281(A): for the grant, "a TAFDC client shall have 100% of his or her earned income disregarded for up to six
-- consecutive months immediately following the start of employment ... provided the total household countable income does
-- not exceed 200% of the Federal Poverty Limit for the client's household size". (B): "After the six month period has ended,
-- a working client shall be eligible for the $200 work-related expense and a 50% earned income disregard." (C): neither
-- disregard where (1) income was reduced, work ended or a job refused without good cause "within the 30 days before the
-- month", (2) income was not reported on time without good cause, (3) the client is employed in FEP, (4) liable but not in
-- the case. 704.270(A): the client gets the $200 "unless eligible for the 100% Earned Income Disregard"; (B)(1) withholds it
-- on the 704.280(A) or (B) facts. 704.500(A) Steps 2 and 3: the 100% disregard, or the $200 then 50%; then dependent care.
GIVEN `e` IS A `My earnings`
      `months of the 100% disregard already used since this job began` IS A NUMBER
      `household countable income` IS A NUMBER
      `200% of the Federal Poverty Limit for my household size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my countable earnings for the grant` MEANS
    IF `the 100% disregard applies`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the larger of` 0 (`after the disregard` MINUS `the dependent care`)
    WHERE
        `no disregard at all` MEANS
                `a 704.280(A) or (B) condition applies` `e`
            OR  `e`'s `employed in the Full Employment Program`
        `the 100% disregard applies` MEANS
                (NOT `no disregard at all`)
            AND `months of the 100% disregard already used since this job began` LESS THAN 6
            AND `household countable income` AT MOST `200% of the Federal Poverty Limit for my household size`
        `the work-related expense` MEANS
            IF `a 704.280(A) or (B) condition applies` `e` THEN 0 ELSE 200
        `after the work-related expense` MEANS `the larger of` 0 (`e`'s `gross monthly earned income` MINUS `the work-related expense`)
        `after the disregard` MEANS
            IF `no disregard at all`
            THEN `after the work-related expense`
            ELSE `after the work-related expense` TIMES 50%
        `the dependent care` MEANS
            IF `a 704.280(A) or (B) condition applies` `e`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the dependent care deduction` (`e`'s `monthly hours worked`) (`e`'s `children two or older in care`) (`e`'s `children under two in care`) (`e`'s `actual monthly cost of dependent care`)

§§ `704.260 -- is my family's income low enough`

-- 704.260(A): "Filing units whose total countable income ... does not exceed the applicable Need Standard ... are eligible."
-- (B)(2): "If the filing unit's income is over the appropriate Need Standard, the assistance unit is ineligible. If ... equal
-- to or is less than the appropriate Need Standard, the assistance unit is eligible."
GIVEN `my countable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `other members' countable earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `countable unearned income of the filing unit` IS A NUMBER
      `the Need Standard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assistance unit passes the income test` IF
    (`my countable earnings` PLUS `other members' countable earned income` PLUS `countable unearned income of the filing unit`) AT MOST `the Need Standard`

§§ `704.500(A) Step 7 -- how much TAFDC my family gets each month`

-- Step 7: "Subtract the result of Step 6 from the applicable Need Standard ... Round this amount down to the next whole
-- dollar. The result, if $10 or greater, but less than the applicable Payment Standard ..., is the amount to be paid monthly.
-- If the result is less than or equal to the applicable Need Standard, but greater than the applicable Payment Standard, the
-- amount to be paid monthly shall equal the applicable Payment Standard. If the result is zero or greater but less than $10,
-- the assistance unit is considered to be receiving assistance, but will not receive a monthly grant. If the result is less
-- than zero, the assistance unit is financially ineligible."
DECLARE `My monthly TAFDC` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly grant of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `receiving assistance, but no monthly grant, because the result is under $10`
    `financially ineligible, because countable income exceeds the Need Standard`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `total countable income` IS A NUMBER
      `the Need Standard` IS A NUMBER
      `the Payment Standard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `My monthly TAFDC`
`the Step 7 grant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the result` LESS THAN 0 THEN `answered` `financially ineligible, because countable income exceeds the Need Standard`
        IF `the result` LESS THAN 10 THEN `answered` `receiving assistance, but no monthly grant, because the result is under $10`
        IF `the result` LESS THAN `the Payment Standard` THEN `answered` (`a monthly grant of` `the result`)
        IF `the result` GREATER THAN `the Payment Standard` AND `the result` AT MOST `the Need Standard` THEN `answered` (`a monthly grant of` `the Payment Standard`)
        OTHERWISE `not covered` `Step 7 of 106 CMR 704.500(A) states no amount when the result equals the Payment Standard, which happens when the family has no countable income (NOTES.md finding 1)`
    WHERE
        `the result` MEANS FLOOR (`the Need Standard` MINUS `total countable income`)

§§ `Questions for the applicant or client`

@export Does my family pass the TAFDC income test when we apply (106 CMR 704.260, with 704.270, 704.275 and 704.280)?
GIVEN `family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TAFDC assistance unit
      `rent allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your assistance unit gets the rent allowance (generally, if you pay rent in private, unsubsidized housing)
      `September 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the month asked about is September 2026
      `children under 19` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible members of the assistance unit are under 19
      `my gross earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross earned income for the month (wages before tax, tips, commissions), in US dollars, leaving out any wages from the Full Employment Program (they are not counted); 0 if you do not work
      `my monthly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a month you work
      `children 2 or older in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children aged 2 or older (or incapacitated members) in your assistance unit you pay for care for while you work
      `children under 2 in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children under 2 in your assistance unit you pay for care for while you work
      `dependent care cost` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay a month for that care, including transport to and from it, in US dollars
      `reduced work without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reduced your income, left your job or refused a real job offer without good cause before the month
      `late income report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed without good cause to report income on time
      `FEP job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed in the Full Employment Program
      `TAFDC in the last 4 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received TAFDC in any of the last four calendar months
      `others' countable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The countable earned income of the other members of your filing unit, after their own deductions, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The filing unit's countable unearned income for the month (for example child support, unemployment compensation, Social Security), in US dollars; not SSI or other noncountable income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my family pass the TAFDC income test` IF
    `the assistance unit passes the income test`
        (`my countable earnings for the income test` (`My earnings` WITH
            `gross monthly earned income`                                IS `my gross earnings`
            `monthly hours worked`                                       IS `my monthly hours`
            `children two or older in care`                              IS `children 2 or older in care`
            `children under two in care`                                 IS `children under 2 in care`
            `actual monthly cost of dependent care`                      IS `dependent care cost`
            `reduced or quit work, or refused a job, without good cause` IS `reduced work without good cause`
            `failed to report income on time without good cause`         IS `late income report`
            `employed in the Full Employment Program`                    IS `FEP job`) `TAFDC in the last 4 months`)
        `others' countable earnings`
        `unearned income`
        (`the Need and Payment Standard` `family size` `rent allowance` `September 2026` `children under 19`)

@export How much TAFDC will my family get this month (106 CMR 704.500(A))?
GIVEN `family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TAFDC assistance unit
      `rent allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your assistance unit gets the rent allowance (generally, if you pay rent in private, unsubsidized housing)
      `September 2026` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the month asked about is September 2026
      `children under 19` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible members of the assistance unit are under 19
      `my gross earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross earned income for the month, in US dollars, leaving out any wages from the Full Employment Program (they are not counted); 0 if you do not work
      `my monthly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a month you work
      `children 2 or older in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children aged 2 or older (or incapacitated members) in your assistance unit you pay for care for while you work
      `children under 2 in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children under 2 in your assistance unit you pay for care for while you work
      `dependent care cost` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay a month for that care, including transport, in US dollars
      `reduced work without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 30 days before the month, you reduced your income, left your job or refused a real job offer without good cause
      `late income report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed without good cause to report income on time
      `FEP job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed in the Full Employment Program
      `months of 100% disregard used` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months your earnings from this job have already been fully disregarded (0 to 6)
      `household countable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's total countable income for the month, in US dollars (used for the 200% of poverty limit on the 100% disregard)
      `200% of poverty` IS A NUMBER @desc 200% of the Federal Poverty Limit for your household size, per month, in US dollars
      `others' countable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The countable earned income of the other members of your filing unit, after their own deductions, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The filing unit's countable unearned income for the month, including deemed income, in US dollars; not SSI or other noncountable income
GIVETH AN `Answer` `My monthly TAFDC`
`How much TAFDC will my family get` MEANS
    `the Step 7 grant`
        (`my countable earnings for the grant` (`My earnings` WITH
            `gross monthly earned income`                                IS `my gross earnings`
            `monthly hours worked`                                       IS `my monthly hours`
            `children two or older in care`                              IS `children 2 or older in care`
            `children under two in care`                                 IS `children under 2 in care`
            `actual monthly cost of dependent care`                      IS `dependent care cost`
            `reduced or quit work, or refused a job, without good cause` IS `reduced work without good cause`
            `failed to report income on time without good cause`         IS `late income report`
            `employed in the Full Employment Program`                    IS `FEP job`) `months of 100% disregard used` `household countable income` `200% of poverty`
          PLUS `others' countable earnings` PLUS `unearned income`)
        (`the Need and Payment Standard` `family size` `rent allowance` `September 2026` `children under 19`)
        (`the Need and Payment Standard` `family size` `rent allowance` `September 2026` `children under 19`)

@export What is the most I can deduct for dependent care from my earnings for TAFDC (106 CMR 704.275)?
GIVEN `my monthly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a month you work
      `children 2 or older in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children aged 2 or older (or incapacitated members) in your assistance unit you pay for care for
      `children under 2 in care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children under 2 in your assistance unit you pay for care for
      `dependent care cost` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay a month for that care, including transport, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much dependent care can I deduct` MEANS
    `the dependent care deduction` `my monthly hours` `children 2 or older in care` `children under 2 in care` `dependent care cost`

§§ `704.235(B)(1) -- reporting changes (only where someone's income is deemed to my family)`

-- 704.235(B)(1): the person whose income is deemed to the filing unit under 704.210(D)(1): "Changes in the person's income
-- must be reported to the Department within ten days." Counted in days from the change (day 0).
DECLARE `TAFDC party` IS ONE OF `the person whose income is deemed to the filing unit`
DECLARE `TAFDC act` IS ONE OF `report the change in income to the Department`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `TAFDC party` `TAFDC act`
`704.235(B)(1) -- a change in deemed income must be reported within ten days` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person whose income is deemed to the filing unit`
    MUST   `report the change in income to the Department`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person whose income is deemed to the filing unit` BECAUSE "a change in deemed income not reported within ten days (106 CMR 704.235(B)(1))"
